Falsifies `file_system_contract::proofs::the_attribute_store_walk_ends`.

The defect: `extended_attribute::store::iter` advances by the name and value alone and skips the seven-byte header, so records overlap.

Expected to fail: `assert!(consumed <= length)`, and the unwinding assertion of the walk's loop.

diff --git a/crates/file_system_contract/src/extended_attribute.rs b/crates/file_system_contract/src/extended_attribute.rs
--- a/crates/file_system_contract/src/extended_attribute.rs
+++ b/crates/file_system_contract/src/extended_attribute.rs
@@ -425,7 +425,7 @@ pub mod store {
             let value = self
                 .blob
                 .get(body + name_len..body + name_len + value_len)?;
-            self.at += record_len(name_len, value_len);
+            self.at += name_len + value_len;
             Some((name, kind, value))
         }
     }
